/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e770d350-fe93-58e5-a551-254f24aea748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1061 618980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d75b1c61-1292-5625-8252-d8c10bae2e1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1061 618981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e6aeea7-0134-5101-a19a-c37ab846bb82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1061 618984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "42fd3643-e43b-5a23-8553-5171fa424230" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1061 618985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89d80bd5-bf3f-5758-a57c-65437a4424dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1061 618989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a6cc496-9cd7-5d8a-b41a-b6ed6646b019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1061 618992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d3e3cfa-978d-5956-a57b-742f51ee2e89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1064 "The region $\\textrm{R},$ shown below, is the area under the graph of $f(x) = 2x+1$ over the interval $[1,3].$ What is the height of the rectangle defined over the same interval that has the same area as $\\textrm{R}?$ \n\n![](images/01/01597200b1f0e147fa8c53b6301d0c8e37208b5a6cce64cf0d9859d1220d8385.png)\n\n \n\nUsing the formula for the area of a trapezoid, we have that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\textrm{Area}\\,(\\textrm{R}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(3+7)(3-1)= 10.}\n$$\n\nFor the rectangle to have the same area, we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =f(c)(3-1) \\\\ f(c) & =5 \\\\ 2c+1 & =5 \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize what we've just done by saying that\n\n$$\n\\int_1^3 (2x +1)\\, \\textrm d x= f(2) \\cdot (3-1).\n$$\n\nThis is an example of the **mean value theorem for integrals**, which states:\n\n*If $f(x)$ is a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, then there exists a number $c$ in that interval such that*\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x)\\, \\textrm d x = f(c) \\cdot (b-a).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1065 986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c1b3241c-c8fd-514f-aa8c-a000710896d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1064 "The **average value** of a continuous function on a closed interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1065 988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1cced554-b7fa-5fd4-b8b5-86c8e0bb4bc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1067 "The Average Value of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295437 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{9\\pi }" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295437 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295437 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e03faf3-3e92-514d-a666-b56caff650f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295558 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "339eefdd-be81-5592-a01a-49ac8b31465b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296765 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "46fed9e6-b6f9-583b-951d-71398609b0ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296876 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296876 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296876 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296876 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186295558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296876 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7617b7a0-eac2-59c6-b90b-60cddec4dd19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1069 "q-316302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9a63b25-eb4e-543f-9169-7fae6ed27cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297458 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{9}}{9})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }[(-1)^{9}-{1}^{9}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-316303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=10x-4$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $6.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0bab2f3-434f-5bc7-bbe6-28166bd448b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297459 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(10x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}(5{x}^{2}-4x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(5{c}^{2}-4c)-0] \\\\ 6 & =5c-4 \\\\ 10 & =5c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315531 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315531 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315531 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46e8b462-2441-51eb-ae60-4aff0a2f6fe7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316437 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316437 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316437 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ed2abe4d-57c0-599d-b2da-3bc3a8e57a74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316716 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "492b509c-6314-53ae-a2da-64e59ff1f2cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316812 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316812 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316812 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316812 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6d94eeb7-653c-5604-8ed4-f4eb869367bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce1dc838-ac3c-58a3-9be3-5a30e3211516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317528 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/df/dfa665cf99f35e5cd2edef04b3f334f0054bbce7fc9b66c519d59d30e77ba2a1.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[0,10],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0199315-7b83-568e-8a38-7bc403eadc2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317532 #edb/ref 1074 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428159 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428159 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1203->1200. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428159 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186048227 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428160 #edb/ref 